 story showcases a different battle  between doc and spider-man than the one  we saw in sam raimi's spider-man 2. in  this case spider-man's consciousness is  swapped with that of dr octopus letting  doc ock run free in spider-man's body  och then takes over peter's life with  the goal of being a better vigilante  than the old spider-man ever was and he  does a pretty good job of it turning him  into the superior spider-man with a new  costume and some mechanical arms doc ock  takes peter's life in a completely new  direction he improves it quite a bit  starting a large tech company called  parker industries  peter eventually gets his body back but  not until after doc gets a doctorate for  peter and makes him the ceo of a company  with hundreds of  employees this comic answers the  question of what would spider-man be  like if he was set in the era of crime  noir pulp comics and apparently he'd  have a black and white suit and use a  handgun to take down his enemies  spider-man noir is a retelling of the  spidey story set in 1933 his origin  story differs from the typical student  turned vigilante though in this version  spidey takes the role of a rugged  investigative reporter during the great  depression this character was actually  given an on-screen appearance and  spider-man into the spider-verse voiced  by nicholas cage these comics showcase  the darker side of spider-man who  regularly shoots his enemies with 45  caliber pistols even killing them in  some cases  one of the most infamous comic book  stories is spider-man one more day in  which peter makes a deal with the devil  mephisto in order to save aunt may from  dying after being shot  mephisto promises to heal aunt may at  the cost of his marriage with mary jane  watson peter agrees and everyone forgets  that mj and peter were married and  ant-may lives  peter however has to live with the fact  that he's no longer married to mj the  love of his life  many people have speculated that this  story could tie into the upcoming  spider-man no way home film because the  trailer seems somewhat similar to  spider-man's wish where everyone forgets  something about the character we'll just  have to wait and see if mephisto makes  an appearance in the movie alongside  doctor strange in this 1970s comic story  spider-man tries to get rid of his  powers thinking they cause more harm  than good instead of taking away his  powers the process instead causes peter  to grow four extra arms giving him the  same number of limbs as an actual spider  peter even alters his suit to fit these  extra limbs continuing to fight crime  and do good as the friendly six-armed  neighborhood spider-man  after fighting and defeating morbius who  is set to appear in a stand-alone film  in january of 2022  peter is able to revert back to his  original spider-man form with the help  of dr connors the comic series marvel  1602 oddly places the character of  spider-man in victorian england this  version of the character is known as the  spider or peter parkwa a spy from  scotland working for sir nicholas fury  the spider has all the same powers as  the traditional spider-man with the  addition of spinnerets on his arms that  produce organic webs similar to toby  maguire's version of spider-man  the biggest difference though is his  frilly 17th century costume which tries  to tie in some of the original spidey's  costume  peter parkout falls in love with  real-life historical figure virginia  dare the first child from england born  in the new world she acts as the story's  gwen stacy even losing her life at the  hands of norman osborne if there are  spiderman from the past obviously there  are some from the future too spider-man  2099 tells the story of miguel o'hara an  engineer at alcomax which is a  tyrannical corporation that basically  controls society in the year 2099  after miguel turns against his employers  alchemix has him scarred and altered  during a dangerous dna experiment this  experiment 